Discovery

K1: Which MQ metrics exist

fetch metric.series, from:-2h
| filter startsWith(metric.key, "ibmmq")
| summarize series = count(), by:{metric.key}
| sort metric.key asc


This confirms the exact keys and shows which ones have enough series to build on. Look for anything about publish/subscribe or filesystems, because 6.7 and 6.8 depend on it.

K2: Dimensions on the main metrics

fetch metric.series, from:-2h
| filter in(metric.key, {"ibmmq.queue_manager.availability", "ibmmq.queue.depth",
                         "ibmmq.queue.oldest_message", "ibmmq.channel.status",
                         "ibmmq.queue_manager.dlq_depth"})
| dedup metric.key


Scroll right and send me the dimension columns. I need to know whether channel metrics have a channel name, a connection name and a queue manager. Any key that doesn't exist won't return a row.

K3: The Claims app → queue manager map, as a standalone list

fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-90d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter contains(event.name, "IBMMQ_APP")
| fieldsAdd apmid = concat("APP", substring(splitString(event.name, "IBMMQ_APP")[1], from:0, to:8))
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| expand eid = affected_entity_ids
| lookup [ fetch `dt.entity.ibmmq:local_queue` | fields id, qName = entity.name ],
         sourceField: eid, lookupField: id, prefix: "lq."
| filter isNotNull(lq.qName)
| summarize alerts = count(), by:{apmid, queueName = lq.qName}
| lookup [
    timeseries d = avg(ibmmq.queue.depth), by:{queue_manager, queue_name}, from:-24h
    | summarize qms = collectDistinct(queue_manager), by:{queue_name}
  ], sourceField: queueName, lookupField: queue_name, prefix: "m."
| expand qm = m.qms
| summarize queues = countDistinctExact(queueName),
            qms    = arrayRemoveNulls(collectDistinct(qm)),
            by:{apmid}
| sort apmid asc


This is the validated mapping from Section 2, kept as a list so we can see which queue managers each app uses. Every Section 6 tile will start from it.

K4: What are the CLM queue managers?

timeseries a = avg(ibmmq.queue_manager.availability, scalar: true),
           by:{queue_manager}, from:-2h
| filter contains(lower(queue_manager), "clm")
| fields queue_manager, availability = a
| sort queue_manager asc


This shows whether the Claims-looking queue managers report availability at all. If they do, we can decide whether to add them as a portfolio-level group.

K5: Active and recent MQ problem types

fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-30d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter dt.davis.is_duplicate == false
| filter contains(event.name, "IBMMQ_APP") or contains(lower(event.name), "queue manager")
      or contains(lower(event.name), "mq")
| summarize problems = count(),
            active   = countIf(event.status == "ACTIVE"),
            sample   = takeFirst(event.name),
            by:{event.category}
| sort problems desc
